 "method": "Expected values are PTMXMLFile_test.cpp literals at the pin (tier 3); the multi-entry writer layout is derived from PTMXMLHandler.cpp:29-38 (tier 4). Escaping, compression, bounds and malformed-input refusals are native policy checks (tier 4). At wave-4 integration an oracle driver (../oracle/integ-F-ptmxml/driver.cpp) linked against the Release install /ceph/ibmi/abi/oliver/opt/openms4-release-bc9cc12-c19e494-174b576 with conda-forge g++ 14.4.0 stored and loaded names holding <, >, &, \" and ' and loaded two hand-written documents, on ibminode06, twice (identical once the per-run temporary directory is masked). The Release PTMXMLFile::store writes such a name unescaped and its own load then fails with a ParseError; reading an escaped name, Xerces splits the text at every reference and PTMXMLHandler::onCharacters assigns rather than appends, so only the last character run survives. tests/ptm_xml.rs asserts both; this writer's escaping is the documented native difference.",
